# Every text file is stored as LF in the repository, whatever the platform's git
# configuration happens to say. Relying on `core.autocrlf` works only for people
# who have it set: a contributor without it commits CRLF, and from then on every
# diff of that file is a whole-file rewrite. Stated here so the guarantee lives in
# the repository instead of in one machine's config. `text=auto` still leaves
# binary files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# License texts are reproduced byte for byte. Git's line-ending conversion would
# change Apache-2.0 from 11358 bytes to 11560 and make it stop matching the
# canonical copy.
LICENSE text eol=lf
